Description: Let word operators be followed by ( ) [ or {
 Twig only treats a word such as "or" or "in" as an operator when the next
 character is whitespace, a parenthesis, "[" or "{" (since Twig 3.1.0, for
 example "a or[b]" and "a in{b: 1}"). twig-lexer 1.0.0 only allows
 whitespace or "(", so it lexed those words as names. Applied at level 3.
 Level 2 keeps upstream's pattern, which also differs from Twig 2.x
 ("(?=[\s()])"); this package never uses level 2, so that is left alone.
Author: Numiko
Origin: other, https://github.com/twigphp/Twig/blob/v3.1.0/src/Lexer.php
Forwarded: not-needed
Twig-Reference: 3.1.0 (lookahead "(?=[\s()\[{])", unchanged up to 3.28.0)
Test: test/fixtures/twig/operators.twig line 13 (parity with Twig 3.28.0); npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-09-23
---
diff --git a/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts b/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
index 1fc64c8..8f53b85 100644
--- a/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
+++ b/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ export class Lexer {
 
                 // an operator that ends with a character must be followed by a whitespace or an opening parenthesis
                 if (new RegExp('[A-Za-z]').test(operator[length - 1])) {
-                    pattern += '(?=[\\s(])';
+                    pattern += this.level === 3 ? '(?=[\\s()\\[{])' : '(?=[\\s(])';
                 }
 
                 // a space within an operator can be any amount of whitespaces
